---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../../styles/demo.css';
import Typo from '../../components/demos/Typo.astro';
---
<Base
  title="How the checksum catches a typo in your seed · BitcoinKeys.guide"
  description="An interactive demonstration of the BIP-39 checksum: change one word in a throwaway seed phrase and watch a wallet reject it before any coins could be lost. Runs entirely in your browser."
  verified="2026-07-29"
>
  <section class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Interactive demo · try it yourself</p>
    <h1>How a typo <span class="accent">gets caught</span></h1>
    <p class="lead">
      When you copy down twelve <a href="/glossary#seed-phrase">seed words</a>, one nagging fear is: what if I write one down wrong?
      Those words carry a built-in safety net called a <strong>checksum</strong>, and <strong>most of the time</strong> it catches
      exactly that — a proper wallet refuses the whole phrase before a single coin is at risk. Generate a throwaway seed and try to
      slip a typo past it. <strong>Then read the part underneath the demo</strong>, because "most of the time" is doing real work in
      that sentence.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <Typo />
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <p class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn" href="/learn/back-up-your-seed">← How to back up your seed</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="/learn/test-your-backup">Testing a backup →</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="/demos">All demos →</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .cta-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.7rem; margin-top: 1.2rem; }
  .btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; background: var(--accent); color: var(--accent-ink); font-weight: 700;
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.9rem; padding: 0.65rem 1rem; border-radius: 0.6rem; text-decoration: none; }
  .btn.ghost { background: transparent; color: var(--text); border: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .btn.ghost:hover { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent); }
</style>

